+# Tasks
+
+## 1. Repository support
+
+- [x] 1.1 Add `OrderRepository.applyCoupon(id, couponCode, discountCents, finalAmountCents)` that updates the three columns; verify with `npm run build`.
+- [x] 1.2 Add `CouponRepository.recordRedemption(...)` and `CouponRepository.incrementUsedCount(code)`; verify with `npm run build`.
+- [x] 1.3 Add a transaction helper on the `Db`/repositories so order update, redemption insert and usage increment commit together; verify the helper rolls back when the wrapped callback throws.
+
+## 2. Redemption service
+
+- [x] 2.1 Add `OrderService.applyCoupon(id, couponCode)` that loads the order and coupon, enforces `ORDER_NOT_FOUND`, `ORDER_NOT_PENDING`, `COUPON_ALREADY_APPLIED`, `COUPON_NOT_FOUND`, eligibility and `min_amount_cents`; verify each error code with a focused test.
+- [x] 2.2 Implement fixed and percentage discount math with the `max_discount_cents` cap and amount clamp; verify expected `discountCents`/`finalAmountCents` for fixed, percent, capped and over-amount cases.
+- [x] 2.3 Persist order, redemption row and incremented `used_count` in one transaction and return the updated order; verify a `usageLimit` 1 coupon is rejected on the second application.
+
+## 3. HTTP wiring
+
+- [x] 3.1 Register `POST /orders/:id/apply-coupon` in `src/routes/orders.ts` and inject the coupon repository into `OrderService` in `src/app.ts`; verify a successful request returns 200 with the updated order.
+- [x] 3.2 Add `tests/apply-coupon.test.ts` covering success (fixed/percent), not found, non-pending, duplicate coupon, disabled/expired/not-yet-valid, usage limit, minimum amount and discount clamping; verify `npm test` passes.
+
+## 4. Verification
+
+- [x] 4.1 Run `npm run build` and `npm test`; confirm the existing suite in `tests/orders.test.ts` is untouched and green.
+
+## Workflow follow-up
+
+- Archive the change once implementation and tests are complete.
